If you are running Windows NT/2000/XP, you can redefine the colors and
set them to the 'proper' colors you'd get under MS-DOS. You can follow
the instructions at http://cec.wustl.edu/~naw1/console_colors.html to
change the colors manually, though the .REG file on that site sets the
colors brighter than normal. Just follow steps 1-10, except instead of
choosing "Properties" in step 2, choose "Defaults" and then
close/re-open the command prompt afterwards. Use the following color
values:

  R   G   B
  0   0   0 (black)
  0   0 165 (dark blue)
  0 165   0 (dark green)
  0 165 165 (teal)
165   0   0 (red)
165   0 165 (purple)
165  82   0 (brown)
165 165 165 (light gray)
 82  82  82 (dark gray)
 82  82 255 (bright blue)
 82 255  82 (bright green)
 82 255 255 (cyan)
255  82  82 (orange)
255  82 255 (magenta)
255 255  82 (yellow)
255 255 255 (white)

You can also 

